What the program actually does: reads one integer with [38;5;10mscanf("%d")[0m, fills a [38;5;10m{int floors; int bedrooms; double bathrooms;}[0m struct with [38;5;10m(x, 3, 2.0)[0m, [38;5;10mmemcpy[0ms it into a raw byte array, and hex-dumps the object representation. So [38;5;10m0[0m → [38;5;10m00000000030000000000000000000040[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The behaviors that needed care rather than a naive translation:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Raw struct representation.** I used [38;5;10m#[repr(C)][0m for [38;5;10mHouse[0m and serialized at the C field offsets (0, 4, 8) with [38;5;10mto_ne_bytes[0m, so the dump reproduces C's layout and native endianness without any [38;5;10munsafe[0m transmute. The [38;5;10m{0}[0m initializer's zeroing of padding is preserved by starting from a zeroed 16-byte buffer.[0m[0m
- **[38;5;10mscanf[0m semantics, not [38;5;10mread_line[0m.** A byte-at-a-time [38;5;10mScanner[0m skips leading whitespace [3mincluding newlines[23m, accepts an optional sign, and ungets the first non-digit instead of swallowing the rest of the line.[0m[0m
- **Failure leaves [38;5;10mx[0m at 0.** On matching failure or EOF the destination is not written, so [38;5;10m""[0m, [38;5;10m"abc"[0m, [38;5;10m"-abc"[0m, and [38;5;10m"- 5"[0m all print the [38;5;10mfloors == 0[0m dump — matching C, where [38;5;10mx[0m keeps its initializer.[0m[0m
- **glibc overflow quirk.** [38;5;10m%d[0m accumulates with [38;5;10mstrtol[0m semantics (saturate at [38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m) and [3mthen[23m truncates to [38;5;10mint[0m. That is why [38;5;10m"9999...9"[0m prints [38;5;10mffffffff[0m (floors [38;5;10m-1[0m) rather than clamping to [38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m. I replicated the saturate-then-truncate order; a straightforward [38;5;10mi32[0m parse would have diverged here.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Verification was my own, not a delegated claim: I compiled [38;5;10mc_src/src/main.c[0m with gcc into [38;5;10m/tmp/cbuild[0m (never writing to [38;5;10mc_src/[0m), then compared [38;5;10mxxd -p[0m of both binaries' stdout across 34 hand-picked edge cases (empty input, sign-only, [38;5;10mINT_MAX±1[0m, [38;5;10mLONG_MAX±1[0m, leading zeros, [38;5;10m0x1f[0m, trailing junk), 400 random signed integers, and 200 random junk-byte inputs — 0 mismatches. [38;5;10mc_src[0m mtimes are unchanged from when I started.[0m[0m
