One caveat worth stating: the struct layout assumption (size 16, [38;5;10mdouble[0m at offset 8) holds for the x86-64 LP64 target I built and tested on. On a target where C would lay the struct out differently, the hex dump would differ — I verified equivalence on this platform only.[0m[0m
